{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-7d9fe66e-0f2b-4b9c-aac7-b746c3041a20-3d9f2db7-7c9a-4578-a799-3d3eb799b99c", :event/time "2026-10-15T02:30:33.242Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "7d9fe66e-0f2b-4b9c-aac7-b746c3041a20", :dependency nil, :parent nil, :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1792031433226-0.p1esqwpzkb50pasuu3", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Deliver bounded lossless review batches with native invocation proof", :source-path "/home/err/.codex/worktrees/cephalon-review-batching/muse/docs/agile/kanban/deliver-bounded-lossless-review-batches-with-native-invocation-proof-c3041a20.md", :status "incoming", :epic nil, :body "## Context\n\nThe human included bounded lossless batching in the finite cephalon B3 prerequisite on2026-10-15, questioncall_1d609fd775e34385958566086e527a3e. Three actual free OpenCode MiMo reviews of the approximately11.8MB/150-input OpenPlanner diff hit the existing two-hour limit; the latest assessed389of1490 pages. Each current page requires a distinct read call and assessment call. This is an owning transport problem, with no credential repair or review-policy waiver involved.\n\nThe plan [bounded-review-batching-20261015](../../notes/bounded-review-batching-20261015.md) binds the actual qualified Musea9 source and personal carrier. This task is only the joint Muse source package. Downstream ETA integration and real OpenPlanner qualification are separately owned sequential allocations, not implied native dependencies on absent cards.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe compiled Muse review plugin and its canonical invocation verifier support bounded lossless multi-page delivery and distinct model-authored assessments for every original page in one actual invocation, retaining native batch/call membership and every context, chronology, stage, submission and publication guard. Existing single-page usage remains valid.\n\n## Scope\n\nAuthor portable law/shape before adapters, domain then orchestration. Add explicit multi-page read and assessment operations to the existing review plugin/session and current canonical verifier. Preserve original page identities and exact UTF16 start/end/text geometry; do not change source selection or page boundaries to manufacture throughput. Read selection returns only complete consecutive pages from a requested first page, with explicit actual membership and next-page identity. Assessment accepts an explicit ordered vector of distinct original page IDs and a substantive model-authored note for each delivered member; one generic note cannot stand for several assessments. The submitted per-page assessment array and complete coverage retain their existing shape.\n\nDerive delivery/assessment observations inside canonical law from actual native calls. Every derived page witness retains original native callID, partID, event position, tool name and actual batch membership; do not create fictional independent host events. Apply LAST across mixed single-page and batch reads, including failed/late calls. Read-after-assessment latches refusal. All input calls must precede the first deterministic stage; all five stages and actual submit binding remain mandatory. Complete staged context must be read through the existing HOST contract, independently of diff batching.\n\nMeasure the complete actual model-visible serialized response, including escaping, page metadata, coverage and custody fields. Use a reviewed bounded response profile supported by the pinned host: source inspection establishes default custom-tool maxima51200UTF8 bytes/2000 newline-separated lines for1.18.31 and1.18.18, but effective overrides must be verified rather than inferred. Select the largest complete prefix within the proven byte, line and cardinality limits. Bound assessment request cardinality and serialized bytes separately; provider argument/context limits are not established by a response cap. If even one complete page cannot fit, or effective limits cannot be established, refuse without delivery credit or publication; never clip, omit or silently change geometry. Actual150-input eligibility and every batch response must be measured. Final size constants/cardinality are implementation choices requiring recorded boundary measurements, not a promised speedup.\n\nKeep prompts and reviewer tool permissions consistent with the new API, final partial batch, empty input, distinct per-page assessments and explicit complete coverage before stage one. Keep tools thin; raw JSON/UTF8/host operations belong in extern, policy in portable law/domain. Reuse existing serializer and strict decoder where appropriate; do not extend unrelated compiler/runtime behavior.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nContinuation across invocations; timeout-only increases; diff exclusions; replacing page assessments with summaries; synthetic host call IDs or approval; changing canonical reviewer identities/cohort/classifier; paid models, model aliases or credential changes; OpenCode daemon/global plugin publication; cephalon runtime/social/deployment/heartbeat changes; altering unrelated historical receipts or native comments. This task neither implements ETA/OpenPlanner consumers nor completes live B1/B2/B3.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Causal RED reproduces the current absence of an accepted lossless batched trace before production changes. Positive controls include existing single-page traces, mixed usage, empty diff, a one-page final batch and a shorter-than-limit final batch. Complete page order/geometry/text concatenates to exactly the independent staged source.\n2. Pure/domain controls independently refuse malformed/unknown/duplicate/conflicting IDs, missing/extra notes, undelivered assessment, malformed metadata and invalid ranges. A batch transition is atomic: any invalid member refuses without partial delivery or assessment state. A substantive per-page note is required; fixtures do not claim model understanding.\n3. Actual serialized UTF8/line measurements cover exact cap and one-over, Unicode/surrogate boundaries, escaping/control characters, long lines, large coverage metadata and assessment arguments. Over-limit responses/requests refuse or select a smaller whole-page prefix before state mutation; clipped/failed native responses supply no accepted coverage. Unsupported effective host limits refuse qualification.\n4. Independent shaped/native invocation controls reject altered membership, order, content/hash/geometry, fabricated or duplicate native callIDs/partIDs, missing pages/assessments, failed calls, reads after assessment, assessments after stage one, changed source/head/base/session/context and partial/final submission. Existing complete-context/read, first-begin, five-stage, full-input, candidate and publisher/submission negatives remain required. Derived witnesses retain real calls, not synthetic per-page host invocations.\n5. Actual compiled plugin invocation and compiled canonical verifier agree on complete membership, exact response limits, immutable original pages and all refusals. Preserve source/envelope byte/hash custody before/after verification. No acceptance route selects weaker legacy verification because a batch appears. Relevant existing suites, full owner gate and lint finish with zero warnings; unavailable authenticated integration remains explicitly unavailable.\n6. Native Rheos readiness follows qualified planning before implementation. Freeze final planning journal prefixes before RED. Source qualifies/merges as one transport-and-verifier package before ETA can consume it. Builds use isolated publication-disabled homes and owned temporary fixtures; preserve watcher limits and running hosts. Final source approval is distinct from real native large-review completion, required downstream.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun causal RED on owned disposable source/trace fixtures, record source identities, exact exits and genuinely failing assertions, then implement law/shape/extern/domain/infra in order. Exercise the actual compiled plugin and exported invocation verifier; repeat the existing full-input/context/cold-host regression scripts and full configured owner gate only as required. No production file substitution may survive fixture cleanup. Record exact source/serialized bytes, caps, native witness relations and independent readbacks; never log secrets/share tokens. Existing receipt/event/reflection prefixes remain byte-identical. Actual free MiMo completion on the unchanged full150-input scope is a later OpenPlanner consumer exit, not a unit-test result.\n\n## Risks and estimate\n\nProposed8 points covers one coherent joint package: state/API atomicity, exact wire sizing, native witness law/decoder and compiled adversarial regression. Shipping read tools without their verifier creates an admission gap, so these are coupled delivery, rather than independent three-point completions. Independent planning review must challenge the estimate/split and testability. ETA2 and OpenPlanner1 are separate proposed follow-on allocations; no native aggregate, readiness or implementation completion is adopted by this prose. Provider throughput remains measured rather than guaranteed; if the actual bounded attempt still fails, retain failure and stop short of qualification rather than add continuation or weaken guards."}, :causal/root "2edd80d6-6a1d-48a5-9740-9909c0e116a7"}
